%N A217318 The number of meandering curves of order n with both extremities covered by their arcs.
%C A217318 A meandering curve of order n is a continuous curve that does not intersect itself yet intersects a horizontal line n times.
%C A217318 The set of meandering curves of order n (A227167) is partitioned into the following three classes: curves with no extremities (A005316), curves with only one extremity (A217310), and curves with both extremities covered by their arcs. - _Hunter Hogan_, Aug 13 2026
%H A217318 Hunter Hogan, <a href="/A217318/b217318.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..44</a> (first 42 terms from Panayotis Vlamos)
%H A217318 Hunter Hogan, <a href="https://github.com/hunterhogan/mapFolding">mapFolding: Create, alter, and optimize algorithms to count meanders, stamp foldings, and map foldings</a>, GitHub repository, (2026).
%H A217318 A. Panayotopoulos and P. Tsikouras, <a href="https://combinatorialpress.com/article/jcmcc/Volume%20046/vol-046-paper%2013.pdf">Properties of meanders</a>, JCMCC 46 (2003), 181-190.
%H A217318 A. Panayotopoulos, P. Vlamos, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s11786-015-0234-0">Partitioning the Meandering Curves</a>, Mathematics in Computer Science (2015) p 1-10.
%F A217318 a(n) = A223095(n) * A000034(n) / 2. - _Andrew Howroyd_, Dec 06 2015
%F A217318 From _Hunter Hogan_, Aug 13 2026: (Start)
%F A217318 a(n) = A227167(n) - A217310(n) - A005316(n).
%F A217318 a(n) = A005316(n) + n*A000682(n) - A000682(n+1) - ((1 - (n mod 2))*(n*A000682(n)/2) + (n mod 2)*A000682(n+1)). (End)
%Y A217318 Cf. A005315.
%Y A217318 Cf. A227167 (meandering curves of order n), A217310 (meandering curves with only one extremity), A005316 (meandering curves with no extremities).
%Y A217318 Cf. A000682 (semi-meandering curves).
%K A217318 nonn,changed
%O A217318 1,5
